# Product images (HARD RULE)

The app never shows raw Shopee photos. Shopee files are GenerateImage references only.

Each SKU (except jibbitz) is four files:

## 1. Hero / card cutout — `public/products/new/{stem}.png`

Used on catalog cards, section tiles, PDP hero (`?cut=1`, rotated −90° over type), color swatches, first carousel slide.

- Canvas **1000×720 RGBA**, transparent corners (no black/white box)
- Single clog, strict **side profile**, toe **RIGHT**
- No floor, no shadow, **no white fringe / halo / checkerboard**
- Camera gold: `public/products/new/classic-white.png`

Opaque listing JPGs on the hero cover the title. Do not put them in `product.image`.

## 2. PDP gallery — `public/products/new/gallery/{stem}-{front|top|heel}.png`

- Canvas **1536×1024 RGB**, white studio
- **front**: three-quarter, ~35°, toe right — gold `gallery/classic-white-front.png`
- **top**: straight top-down, toe right — gold `gallery/classic-white-top.png`
- **heel**: rear three-quarter — gold `gallery/classic-white-heel.png`

## After a Shopee link

Follow the **shopee-catalog-images** skill, then the **product-image-gen** subagent.

1. Download every listing photo (do not pick one and ignore the rest).
2. Classify angle + colorway. Keep identity refs per SKU.
3. Generate all four files. `reference_image_paths` = Shopee identity photos + the gold camera file for that view.
4. Prefer GenerateImage over rembg / flood-cut when edges look dirty.
5. Do not ship left-facing cutouts. Flip in the prompt (toe right), not by shipping a left-facing PNG.
6. Do not install rembg/onnx/playwright unless the user asks.
7. Do not generate from the product name alone. Do not use a previous AI tile as the identity ref.

## Quality gate (before saying done)

Open the actual PNG in the UI:

- cutout: toe on the **right**, no halo on `#f7f7f8` cards, no box on `#f3f4f7` hero
- gallery: same clog as the listing, correct named view
